FeatureName: Keyboard Shortcuts for Tool Selection (Accessibility Feature)

Description:
		This feature allows users to quickly switch between different drawing tools
    	using keyboard shortcuts. Each shape button, including the Select/Move tool,
    	has an assigned shortcut key (e.g., C for Circle, R for Rectangle, S for Square,
    	T for Triangle, O for Oval, Q for Squiggle, L for Polyline, M for Select/Move, etc).
    	When a user presses one of these keys, the corresponding tool becomes active
    	instantly.

    	Additionally, each button displays its shortcut key in brackets beside its name
    	and shows the shortcut when hovered over, making it clear and intuitive for users
    	to learn and use the hotkeys efficiently.

    	Accessibility Benefits:
    	The introduction of keyboard shortcuts also improves accessibility for users who
    	may have difficulty using a mouse or performing precise pointer movements. People
    	with limited motor control, hand tremors, or repetitive strain injuries benefit from
    	being able to switch tools without needing to click small UI buttons. Keyboard navigation
    	reduces reliance on fine motor skills and provides an alternative input method for users
    	who cannot effectively use a mouse. By offering both visual tool selection and efficient
    	keyboard access, the feature supports a wider range of user needs and interaction preferences.

