FeatureName: Undo/Redo Functionality

Description:
        This feature implements full Undo and Redo support for the paint
        application. Any canvas-modifying action—such as drawing a shape,
        moving a shape, changing color or fill style, erasing, cutting,
        copying, pasting, or adding text—is wrapped inside a Command and
        recorded in the command history.

        When the user presses Undo, the most recent command is undone and the
        canvas immediately reflects the previous state. When the user presses
        Redo, the undone command is reapplied and restored on the canvas.
        The system supports multiple consecutive undos/redos and behaves like
        a professional drawing program.

        This allows users to freely reverse mistakes, restore actions, and
        maintain full control over their editing workflow.

